00:03:48.250 --> 00:04:02.660
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): Governance is the set of operations intended to mitigate risks by holding a set of actors accountable over a set of rules or laws. Governance shows up everywhere, in governments, standards organizations, game administration, and even in families.

28
00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:09.879
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): Wherever there's a need to manage behavior, reduce risk, or enforce fairness, governance provides the structure to make that possible.

29
00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:17.489
